Don't pass MSG_WAITALL to recv() on the network input socket.

On Cygwin, recv() with MSG_WAITALL does not return when the peer has closed
the connection after sending only part of the requested block, so the
receiving mbuffer never sees the end of the stream and hangs in CLOSE_WAIT.
readBlock() already loops until a whole block has been read (and handles
0 as end-of-file), so a plain recv() is equivalent.

diff --git a/input.c b/input.c
--- a/input.c
+++ b/input.c
@@ -292,7 +292,7 @@
 		if (IDevBSize)
 			in = devread(at,num);
 		else if (InSocket)
-			in = recv(In,Buffer[at] + num,Blocksize - num,MSG_WAITALL);
+			in = recv(In,Buffer[at] + num,Blocksize - num,0);
 		else
 			in = read(In,Buffer[at] + num,Blocksize - num);
 		debugiomsg("inputThread: read(In, Buffer[%d] + %llu, %llu) = %d\n", at, num, Blocksize - num, in);
